## REDIS AS A SHARED DISTRIBUTED CACHE
---------------------------------------

Ek microservice ki multiple instances same external Redis Cache
ko access kar sakti hain.

For example, Product Service ki multiple instances hain:

    P1, P2, P3

In sab instances ke liye ek shared Redis Cache configured ho sakta hai.


## EXAMPLE
-----------

Suppose client request bhejta hai:

    GET /products/101


Request API Gateway aur Product Load Balancer ke through
Product Service ki kisi instance, for example P1, tak pahunchti hai.


    Client
       ↓
    API Gateway
       ↓
 Product Load Balancer
       ↓
      P1


P1 request receive karne ke baad defined naming convention ke
basis par Cache Key construct karti hai:

    product:101


P1 shared Redis Cache me is key ke corresponding data check karti hai.


### CASE 1: CACHE HIT
---------------------

Agar `product:101` ke corresponding data Cache me available hai:

    P1
     ↓
Shared Redis Cache
     ↓
  Cache Hit
     ↓
Return Cached Data


Is case me Database ko hit karne ki zarurat nahi padti.


### CASE 2: CACHE MISS
----------------------

Agar `product:101` Cache me available nahi hai:

    P1
     ↓
Shared Redis Cache
     ↓
  Cache Miss
     ↓
Product Database
     ↓
Fetch Product Data
     ↓
Store Data in Redis

Application retrieved data ko usi Cache Key:

    product:101

ke against shared Redis Cache me store kar deti hai aur
response client ko return kar deti hai.


## NEXT REQUEST
----------------

Ab suppose same request dobara aati hai:

    GET /products/101


Is baar Load Balancer request ko kisi doosri instance,
for example P3, tak route kar sakta hai.


    Client
       ↓
Product Load Balancer
       ↓
      P3


P3 bhi same defined naming convention ke basis par
same Cache Key construct karegi:

    product:101


P3 shared Redis Cache me is key ko check karegi.

Kyunki P1 pehle hi `product:101` ke corresponding data ko
Redis me store kar chuki hai:

    P3
     ↓
Shared Redis Cache
     ↓
  Cache Hit
     ↓
Return Cached Data


Database ko dobara hit karne ki zarurat nahi padegi.


## IMPORTANT
-------------

Isliye Redis jaise external cache ko multiple service instances ke
beech ek shared distributed cache ke roop me use kiya ja sakta hai.

Ek instance dwara Cache me store kiya gaya data, doosri instances bhi
same Cache Key ke through access kar sakti hain.

Yahi Redis ko horizontally scaled applications me useful banata hai,
kyunki multiple instances ek hi shared Cache layer ko use kar sakti hain.





