## STALE-WHILE-REVALIDATE
---------------------------

Ye bhi ek approach hai jo popular cache entry ke expire hone ke
baad Cache Stampede ko prevent karne ke liye use ki ja sakti hai.

Basically normal caching scenario me har cache key ke saath ek TTL
(Time To Live) associated hota hai.

TTL expire hone ke baad corresponding key Redis se remove ho jaati hai.

Agar usi time us key ke corresponding data ke liye bahut saari concurrent requests aati hain,
to sabko Cache Miss mil sakta hai aur multiple requests backend /
Database ko hit kar sakti hain.


Stale-While-Revalidate approach me hum cache entry ki lifetime ko
logically do periods me divide karte hain:

    1. Fresh Time
    2. Stale Time


Example:

Database me:

    product:101
    price = ₹79,999


Hum is data ko Redis me cache karte hain.

Ab hum decide karte hain:

    Fresh Time = 10 minutes
    Stale Time = 5 minutes


Matlab:

First 10 minutes tak data ko fresh maana jayega.

Uske baad next 5 minutes tak data technically stale hoga,
lekin temporarily client ko serve karna allowed hoga.


So cache entry ko total:

10 min Fresh
      +
5 min Stale
--------------
15 minutes

tak Redis me available rakhna hoga.

Conceptually:

Redis TTL = Fresh Time + Stale Time

Yahan:

    Redis TTL = 15 minutes


## TIMELINE:
-------------

Suppose data 10:00 AM par Redis me store hua.


    10:00 → 10:10

    Data = Fresh


    10:10 → 10:15

    Data = Stale, but still available in Redis
    and temporarily serve kiya ja sakta hai.


    After 10:15

    Redis TTL expire ho sakta hai aur cache key
    Redis se remove ho jaayegi.


## REDIS KO KAISE PATA CHALEGA KI DATA STALE HAI?
------------------------------------------------------

Yahan ek important point hai.

Redis ko sirf apni key ka actual TTL pata hota hai.

Suppose humne decide kiya:

Fresh Time = 10 minutes
Stale Time = 5 minutes

To Redis key ka total TTL ho sakta hai:

10 min + 5 min = 15 minutes

Redis ke perspective se:

product:101
TTL = 15 minutes

yaani, Redis ke liye key simply 15 minutes tak exist karegi aur uske baad expire ho jayegi.

Redis ko ye nahi pata hota ki:

First 10 minutes → Fresh

Next 5 minutes → Stale

Isliye freshness determine karne ki responsibility application ki hoti hai.

Application ko separately track karna padega ki data kab tak fresh maana jayega.

For example, Redis me conceptually:

Key:

product:101
{
    "data": {
        "id": 101,
        "price": 79999
    },
    "freshUntil": "10:10 AM"
}

Aur Redis key ka actual:

TTL = 15 minutes


Ab application request ke time:

Current Time < freshUntil
        ↓
     Fresh Data

Aur:

Current Time > freshUntil
        ↓
     Stale Data

Lekin jab tak Redis key ka 15-minute TTL expire nahi hota, stale data Redis me available rahega aur application usse temporarily serve kar sakti hai.


