## 16 : CACHE AVALANCHE
==========================

Normal caching me different data Cache me store hota hai aur
har cache entry ke saath TTL configured ho sakta hai.

Suppose application ne bahut saare products approximately
ek hi time par Cache me store kiye:

    product:101 → TTL = 10 min
    product:102 → TTL = 10 min
    product:103 → TTL = 10 min
    product:104 → TTL = 10 min


Agar ye entries approximately same time par Cache me store hui hain
aur in sabke liye similar TTL configured hai, to inki TTL bhi
approximately same time par expire ho sakti hai.

Result:

    product:101 → Expired
    product:102 → Expired
    product:103 → Expired
    product:104 → Expired


Ab agar different products ke liye bahut saari requests aati hain:

    Request → product:101 → Cache Miss
    Request → product:102 → Cache Miss
    Request → product:103 → Cache Miss
    Request → product:104 → Cache Miss


Result:

        Many Cache Entries Expire
                  ↓
           Many Cache Misses
                  ↓
        Many Database Requests
                  ↓
          Database Load Spike


Cache Avalanche ek aisi situation hai jahan bahut saari Cache entries ek saath ya approximately same time par expire ya unavailable ho jaati hain. 
Is wajah se bahut saari different cache keys ke liye aane wali requests Cache Miss encounter karti hain aur data fetch karne ke liye Database tak pahunch jaati hain. 
Isse Database par sudden load spike aa sakta hai.


---------------------------
## SOLUTION : TTL JITTER
---------------------------

Cache Avalanche me problem tab hoti hai jab bahut saari cache entries 
ek hi ya similar time par expire ho jaati hain.

Humara aim hai ki unki expiration ko different time periods me spread out kiya ja sake, 
taaki ek saath bahut zyada Cache Misses na hon aur Database par sudden load spike ka risk reduce ho.

## CORE IDEA :
---------------

Jab bhi koi nayi cache entry create ya update hoti hai,
us time Base TTL ke saath thoda random variation add kar diya
jata hai. Isse cache entries different times par expire hoti hain.

## EXAMPLE
------------

Base TTL = 10 minutes

Jitter = Random(0–2 minutes)

Actual TTL:

    Base TTL + Random Jitter


Har new cache entry ke liye TTL independently calculate ho sakti hai:


product:101

Created at → 10:00:00
TTL        → 10 min + 43 sec


product:102

Created at → 10:00:05
TTL        → 10 min + 1 min 27 sec


product:103

Created at → 10:00:12
TTL        → 10 min + 18 sec


Isliye in cache entries ka expiration bhi different times par
hoga.


## CONCEPTUALLY :
------------------

    Different Expiration Times
              ↓
      Cache Misses Spread Out
              ↓
    Database Requests Spread Out
              ↓
Database par sudden load spike ka
risk reduce hota hai


## WHEN IS TTL JITTER USEFUL ?
-------------------------------

TTL Jitter especially useful hota hai jab bahut saari cache
entries similar time window me populate ho rahi hon aur unke
expire hone ka time synchronize ho sakta ho.

Examples:

    - Application startup / cache warm-up
    - Batch processing
    - Bulk caching
    - Kisi event ke baad multiple cache entries populate hona





