## 19 : CACHE WARMING / PREWARMING
=====================================

Kuch situations me hume pehle se pata hota hai ki kisi particular time
par kuch popular products ke liye bahut zyada traffic aane wala hai.

-------------
### EXAMPLE:
-------------

Black Friday Sale → 10:00 AM

Agar Sale start hone ke time popular products ki Cache entries empty
ya expired hain:

Users
   ↓
Application
   ↓
Cache Miss
   ↓
Database


Ab maan lo kisi ek popular product ke liye bahut saari concurrent
requests aati hain aur sabhi requests Cache Miss encounter karti hain.
Ye requests ek saath Database tak pahunch sakti hain, jisse Database
par sudden load spike aa sakta hai aur Cache Stampede jaisi situation
create ho sakti hai.

Agar ek saath bahut saare different products ki Cache entries bhi
Miss ho rahi hain, to Cache Avalanche jaisi situation create ho sakti hai.

------------------------------
## SOLUTION : CACHE WARMING
------------------------------

Cache Warming / Prewarming ka matlab hai expected-to-be-frequently
accessed data ko actual user requests aane se pehle proactively Cache
me populate kar dena.

Example:

Black Friday Sale start hone wali hai
↓
System identifies popular products
↓
Fetch Data from Database
↓
Populate Redis Cache
↓
Sale Starts
↓
User Requests
↓
Cache Hit
↓
Return Data

Is case me Cache ko populate karne ke liye actual user requests ke
Cache Miss hone ka wait nahi karna padta.

Data pehle se Cache me available hota hai.

---------------------------------
## CACHE WARMING KA MAIN BENEFIT
---------------------------------

Isliye Cache Warming ka main purpose hai:

Agar kisi particular product ke liye **expected high traffic** hai, to uska data pehle hi Cache me populate kar diya jata hai, 
taaki initial requests Cache Miss encounter karke unnecessarily Database ko overload na karein.





